{"book":8,"chapter":1,"context":{"chapter":1,"title":"Where You Go, I Will Go","summary":"Famine drives Naomi's family to Moab, where she loses her husband and both sons. Heading home, she urges her Moabite daughters-in-law to stay; Orpah does, but Ruth vows to go with Naomi and make Naomi's God her own.","background":"There is irony in the setting: Bethlehem means 'house of bread,' yet it has no food. Moab was an old rival of Israel (Deuteronomy 23:3). A widow with no sons had no secure income or protector, which is why Naomi urges the younger women to go home and remarry. 'Naomi' means 'pleasant'; 'Mara,' the name she asks to be called, means 'bitter' (v. 20).","customs":[{"term":"Sons for your husbands","verses":"1:11-13","note":"Naomi alludes to the custom of a dead man's brother marrying his widow (Deuteronomy 25:5-6). She has no sons left to offer, and is too old to bear more."}],"watchFor":["The word 'return' runs through the chapter.","Ruth's pledge: 'thy people shall be my people, and thy God my God' (vv. 16–17).","'I went out full... home again empty' (v. 21), yet they arrive as barley harvest begins (v. 22)."],"connections":["Genesis 19:36-37","Deuteronomy 23:3","Deuteronomy 25:5-6","Matthew 1:5"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיְהִי","vayhi","H1961","Hc/Vqw3ms","and it was"],["בִּימֵי","bimei","H3117","HR/Ncmpc","in [the] days of"],["שְׁפֹט","shefot","H8199","HVqcc","[the] judging of"],["הַשֹּׁפְטִים","hashofetim","H8199","HTd/Vqrmpa","the judges"],["וַיְהִי","vayhi","H1961","Hc/Vqw3ms","and it was"],["רָעָב","ra'av","H7458","HNcmsa","a famine"],["בָּאָרֶץ","ba'aretz","H776","HRd/Ncfsa","in the land"],["וַיֵּלֶךְ","vaiyelekh","H1980","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he went"],["אִישׁ","'ish","H376","HNcmsa","a man"],["מִבֵּית","mibeit","H1035","HR/Npl","from Beth-"],["לֶחֶם","lechem","H1035","HNpl","-lehem"],["יְהוּדָה","yehudah","H3063","HNpl","Judah"],["לָגוּר","lagur","H1481","HR/Vqcc","to sojourn"],["בִּשְׂדֵי","bisdei","H7704","HR/Ncmpc","in [the] region<s> of"],["מוֹאָב